---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PRO_PRICE } from '../lib/store';

// The structural / brand sections (stack, principles, what's-coming) are
// drafted from screen_draw/docs/ROADMAP.md context. The personal-voice
// sections (intro, why-built-it) are written pseudonymously (handle: vijo);
// edit freely if any detail doesn't match your actual story.

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout
  title="Limnia · About"
  description="Who built Limnia and why."
>
  <main class="relative z-10">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-24 sm:px-10 sm:pt-28">
      <header class="mb-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint md:col-span-3">
          / about
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-9">
          <h1 class="font-display text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.03] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[56px]">
            About.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
            What Limnia is, who made it, what's next.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <article class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">

        {/* ─── Main column: prose ─── */}
        <div class="space-y-12 lg:col-span-8">

          <section>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint">
              hi
            </p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
              I'm vijo.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              I'm an independent developer in Sweden, and Limnia is a solo
              project: one person, no company, no funding. I built it because
              I wanted it to exist, and I use it every day. The app and this
              site are the whole operation.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint">
              why this exists
            </p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
              The thing I needed didn't exist.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              It started in screen shares. I kept circling things with the
              mouse cursor, wobbling it around a line of code or a corner of
              a slide, hoping the other person could tell what I meant. What
              I wanted was a pen. Not an app, not a canvas, not a feature
              that lives inside one meeting tool and not the others. A pen
              for the screen itself: press a key, draw on whatever is there,
              press it again and it's gone.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              The existing tools each have a piece of it. ZoomIt can draw,
              but it's a zoom utility first and drawing feels like a detour.
              Epic Pen parks a toolbar on your screen all day. ShareX
              annotates screenshots after the fact, which is great for bug
              reports and useless mid-conversation. None of them treat
              disappearing as the core feature. That was the part I cared
              about most, so I built the tool around it: a click-through
              overlay that is invisible until you need it and gone the
              moment you don't.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint">
              what it's made of
            </p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
              <span class="text-pen">Rust</span>, Win32, and a lot of
              respect for your screen.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              Limnia is written in Rust (edition 2024) against the raw Windows
              API. No Electron. No web view. The drawing overlay uses no GPU.
              Every stroke is composited in software. The whole binary is
              <span class="font-mono text-[14.5px] text-ink">~2 MB</span>.
              Settings live in a JSON file in your AppData folder, and Pro
              licenses are verified entirely offline (Ed25519, no server).
              Crashes write to a local log file you choose whether to share.
              Nothing else gets written; nothing leaves the machine.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              The source is closed. That's a deliberate choice. Solo-dev
              overhead of dual-repo + license management is meaningful, and
              the closest comparables in this category (Epic Pen, ZoomIt) are
              also closed. The
              <a href={`${base}/changelog`} class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">changelog</a>
              is public so you can see exactly what shipped and when.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint">
              free and pro
            </p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
              Free stays free. Pro is additive.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              Every feature shipped today stays in the free tier, forever.
              The Pro tier ({PRO_PRICE} one-time) is already built into the
              app: MP4 and GIF recording for streamers, whiteboard and
              blackboard canvases for teachers, a magnifier and region
              capture for pointing at the small stuff. None of it changes
              what Free does.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
              Pro is not on sale quite yet; checkout opens on the
              <a href={`${base}/#pricing`} class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">pricing page</a>
              once the store goes live, and the full feature split is there
              today. There are no subscriptions, no cloud services, and no
              plans for either. If you need Limnia for commercial work
              (client deliverables, paid courses), a separate Commercial
              Use License will exist alongside Pro.
            </p>
          </section>

        </div>

        {/* ─── Sidebar: contact + support ─── */}
        <aside class="space-y-8 lg:col-span-4">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint">
              contact
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 font-mono text-[12.5px]">
              <li class="grid grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] items-baseline gap-2">
                <span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">github</span>
                <a href="https://github.com/vijo0018" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink hover:text-pen">vijo0018 <span class="opacity-60">↗</span></a>
              </li>
              <li class="grid grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] items-baseline gap-2">
                <span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">issues</span>
                <a href="https://github.com/vijo0018/limnia-site/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink hover:text-pen">github / issues <span class="opacity-60">↗</span></a>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[12px] leading-[1.5] text-ink-faint">
              GitHub is the fastest way to reach me. Press inquiries welcome
              through either channel.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint">
              support development
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-muted">
              If Limnia earns its place in your workflow, a tip funds the
              code-signing certificate and the cups of coffee that go into
              the next release.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 grid gap-2">
              <a
                href="https://github.com/sponsors/vijo0018"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="group flex items-center justify-between rounded-md border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-ink transition-colors hover:border-laser/40 hover:bg-laser/5"
              >
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="text-laser">♥</span>
                  Sponsor on GitHub
                </span>
                <span class="font-mono text-[11px] opacity-60 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">↗</span>
              </a>
              <a
                href="https://ko-fi.com/vijo0018"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="group flex items-center justify-between rounded-md border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-2.5 text-[13.5px] text-ink transition-colors hover:border-highlight/40 hover:bg-highlight/5"
              >
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="text-highlight">☕</span>
                  Buy a coffee
                </span>
                <span class="font-mono text-[11px] opacity-60 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">↗</span>
              </a>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">
              ♥ donor before pro goes on sale? pro is yours at launch.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint">
              press kit
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-muted">
              Logos, screenshots, and pre-written copy for journalists and
              bloggers.
            </p>
            <a
              href={`${base}/press/`}
              class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[12px] text-ink hover:text-pen"
            >
              /press <span class="opacity-60">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </aside>

      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
